{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794408106,"nonce":"YLHOc23ei0QrWAkDehb2HwIPFsY=","message":"How opaque values are passed was decided with the user on 2026-11-11 and is written up in docs/design.md under \"Passing handles\". One Haxe object owns one handle; a parameter is only ever borrowed, a result is always owned.\n\nBuilt into the generator, which covers item 4 of the list above in part:\n\n- An interface as a parameter: `\u0026T` (shared) or `\u0026mut T` (exclusive), of the same interface or another.\n- An interface as the result of any function, not only `new`. The Haxe side makes a new object of that interface's class to own it; on hxcpp the object takes ownership only once the library has handed the value over.\n- `Option` of either, as null.\n- `self` by value, which takes the value out and so closes the Haxe object.\n- A null object is passed as a null handle whether or not the library takes one, and the library refuses it. This is the same error on both runtimes, and it is needed on hxcpp, which reads the field of a null object without checking: the first version segfaulted there.\n\nTested through `Generated.hx` (`absorb`, `swap`, `fork`, `larger`, `into_value`, and a second interface `Tally` that takes and makes counters) on Ash in hybrid, jit and interp modes, stock HashLink and hxcpp: the same object passed twice with one exclusive use is \"in use\"; a consumed object is closed and its value gone; everything made is released.\n\nDecided but not built:\n\n- Sharing. A library that hands the same thing out twice returns something clonable, each return being its own handle. Nothing in the generator knows about `Arc`; a library does this in its own types today.\n- Haxe values held by Rust: an id, with the table kept by the binding.\n- CPPIA: an id table in the host in place of a raw pointer.\n\nStill refused by the generator: an interface taken by value as a parameter, a result that borrows, lists of interfaces, more than one source file, free functions outside an `impl`.","files":null}]}